{"repositoryId":1291584788,"availability":"available","full":"pranjal020496/sugarbelly","name":"sugarbelly","description":"An interactive data app that combines publicly available obesity and sugar availability data, using machine learning to forecast how obesity scenarios may change by 2030 under different sugar availability assumptions.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-06T23:46:32Z","updated":"2026-07-08T14:38:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sugarbelly-pranjal020496.streamlit.app/","topics":["data-science","forecasting","machine-learning","plotly","postgresql","scikit-learn","sql","streamlit"],"demo":"https://sugarbelly-pranjal020496.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T04:05:34.405Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T04:05:34.405Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T04:05:34.405Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T00:54:45.811Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-20T04:05:34.405Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sugar Belly is an end-to-end data analytics and machine learning application that explores global obesity trends, country-level sugar and sweeteners availability, and forward-looking obesity risk scenarios across countries and WHO regions.","The project combines data engineering, PostgreSQL analytics, SQL-based feature engineering, interactive dashboarding, machine learning model benchmarking, and sugar-sensitivity forecasting to 2030.","Important interpretation note: This project analyzes associations and forecast scenarios, not causation. FAOSTAT sugar values represent national food supply availability, not exact individual-level consumption."],"features":["The project uses PostgreSQL tables and SQL views to create a reusable analytics foundation.","vsugarobesitycountryyear","vsugarobesityregionsummary","vsugarobesitycountrychange","vmlsugarsensitivityfeatures"],"sourceUrl":"https://g